      <rules>
        <rule name="Missing Pay" id="0965-b1ba-d49c-5b3c" hidden="false">
          <description>If one of your chieftains dies, your warriors suffer a -1 penalty to the ensuing morale check. That means that your warriors will flee the battlefield on a result of 1 or 2.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Mounted Archers" id="2299-5329-f82e-eb7e" hidden="false">
          <description>Roman cavalry can be equipped with bows. Their use imposes the same constraints on cavalry as it does on infantry (see the rulebook, p.45).</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Symbol of Rome" id="a039-0024-6c27-743b" hidden="false">
          <description>Roman banners follow the same rules as ordinary banners (see the rulebook, p.79). 


**However, instead of allowing to hit rolls of 1 to be re-rolled, this banner lets you re-roll all failed defense rolls instead.**</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Death to the False Emperor" id="c5c9-88c4-8a99-f8ae" hidden="false">
          <description>If you field this faction against this faction (i.e. either Western or Eastern Romans), you can re-roll all your rolls to hit the enemy chieftain or chieftains.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </forceEntry>
  </forceEntries>
